# trouble v0.1 environment file (SPEC-12).
# This file must be mode 0600. Put secrets here, never on the command line.
# Full surface: docs/reference/env-vars.md (derived twins + literal exceptions).

# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Values, never names, and never on argv. Each variable below is what the
# matching `*_env` config key points at; the key holds the VARIABLE NAME.
# Example hub token (satellite mode; the env twin of the config key `hub.token`):
# TROUBLE_HUB_TOKEN=sk_live_...
# Example dashboard bearer token (written by `trouble dashboard token create`):
# TROUBLE_DASHBOARD_TOKEN=dsh_...
# Redis password for `server.profile = light-hub` (default of server.redis.password_env):
# TROUBLE_REDIS_PASSWORD=...
# DuckBrain key for the duckbrain issue driver and the hub ledger archive:
# TROUBLE_DUCKBRAIN_KEY=...
# GitHub token for the github issue driver:
# TROUBLE_GITHUB_TOKEN=...
# Flow router dispatch token ([flow] router.token_env):
# TROUBLE_ROUTER_TOKEN=...

# --- non-secret overrides ----------------------------------------------------
# Every config key also has a derived twin (TROUBLE_ + upper(key), `.`/`-` -> `_`),
# and these literals are read directly by their subsystem; see the reference page.
# TROUBLE_STATE_ROOT=/home/<user>/.local/state/trouble
# TROUBLE_CONFIG_PATH=/home/<user>/.config/trouble/config.toml
